"""Library entries vendored from Metasploit Framework payloads and encoders.

The bytes here were generated once, offline, through the Metasploit Framework's
own API (the same path msfvenom uses): every single (stageless) native
x86/x64/arm64 payload across all supported OSes, plus every x86/x64 encoder's
real decoder stub (shikata_ga_nai excluded on request). Network payloads were
generated with a dummy LHOST 127.0.0.1 / LPORT 4444 and exec payloads with a
dummy command (/bin/sh or cmd.exe); edit those in the editor to retarget.

Nothing here runs Metasploit at runtime: the bytes are static and vendored in
``_DATA`` below. Each payload is offered as *editable assembly* when our own
disassembly reassembles to the exact same bytes (so the asm column is faithful
source you can edit); otherwise it falls back to loading as raw bytes, which the
editor disassembles. Encoder decoder-stubs always load as raw bytes.
"""

